Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 21:38:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 019/154] atrium: expose edit-focus state so hotkeys can be
 gated on it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two features were blocked on not being able to answer 'is the user typing?':
Cmd+Shift+Arrow for workspace switching and Cmd+F for the sidebar
filter. Both are standard macOS text-editing chords, and binding
either without a focus signal would steal keystrokes from every text field.

The signal is content::WebContents::IsFocusedElementEditable(), the public
projection of the same renderer state that drives the virtual keyboard.
TextInputManager would have been richer but lives in content/browser and
chrome/browser/DEPS permits only content/public/browser; there is no public
accessor for ui::TextInputType. The imprecision errs toward over-blocking - a
readonly input reads as editable.

Read live rather than cached. A cache diverges in a case no notification
covers: dragging a tab with a focused field into another window reparents
native views without moving DOM focus, so nothing fires and the destination
reads 'nothing focused' while the caret is still in the field. The observer
now only triggers a re-push to Swift.

Gating is a property of the CHORD, not the action, so a rebind onto a
text-editing chord is gated with no per-action policy. Both dispatch routes
are covered: prePerformKeyEquivalent falls through to super rather than
dropping, so a declined key still travels. Fails closed on an unresolved
signal, an unknown kind, or a snapshot from another tab.

New ABI group appended at the tail (ninth group); the frozen content/shell
copy is untouched.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
index 205b3838feda3..bf62c173ffe71 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
@@ -619,6 +619,7 @@ static_library("ui") {
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:devtools_card_corners",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:devtools_pane_selection",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:extension_actions_json",
+    "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:edit_focus_gate",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:extension_popup_watchdog_policy",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:little_marker",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:routing_navigation_decision",
